data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default"><div class="elementor-widget-container"><p><b>How long does it typically take to build a D2C app?</b></p><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The development timeline varies depending on the app's complexity and the resources available. A basic app might take 2-3 months, while a more complex one with custom features could take 6-9 months or longer. It's crucial to plan for development, testing, and deployment to ensure a smooth launch.</span></p><p><b>Do I need to build separate apps for iOS and Android?</b></p><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It depends on your target audience and budget. If you want to reach the widest possible audience, developing for both platforms is ideal. However, if resources are limited, you can start with one platform (usually the one your target customers use most) and expand later. Hybrid app development (using frameworks like React Native or Flutter) can also be a cost-effective option for reaching both platforms.</span></p><p><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p></div></div>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":false},{"id":"24ffb9b","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":33,"_inline_size":23.171,"hide_tablet":"hidden-tablet","hide_mobile":"hidden-mobile"},"elements":[{"id":"a71312e","elType":"section","settings":{"height_inner":"min-height","sticky":"top","sticky_offset":100,"sticky_effects_offset":100,"sticky_parent":"yes","the7_sticky_row_overlap":"yes","the7_hide_on_sticky_effect":"show"},"elements":[{"id":"2d5d6a1","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null,"css_classes":"stickForm","hide_tablet":"hidden-tablet","custom_css":".stickForm{
